WEBVTT

00:11.810 --> 00:13.830
Ken-chan!

00:16.620 --> 00:19.750
Ken-chan! Where are you?

00:19.810 --> 00:21.940
I brought watermelons.

00:27.710 --> 00:28.870
Ken-chan?

00:31.110 --> 00:34.370
Ah, you're messing with uncle's motorcycle.

00:34.410 --> 00:36.290
You'll get in trouble.

00:37.010 --> 00:38.100
Ken-chan?

00:38.310 --> 00:41.580
Don't worry, this is my bike now.

00:42.110 --> 00:43.220
Really?

00:43.310 --> 00:46.580
Yeah, dad said he'd give it to me when I grow up.

00:46.910 --> 00:49.190
So I have to make it clean.

00:52.510 --> 00:54.110
Hey, Ken-chan...

00:54.110 --> 00:55.000
No!

00:55.120 --> 00:57.140
I haven't said anything.

00:57.710 --> 01:02.130
"Ken-chan, I want to have a ride," right?

01:02.210 --> 01:04.880
Wow, how did you know?

01:04.910 --> 01:06.560
That's because I know!

01:09.960 --> 01:11.220
That's so nice.

01:13.110 --> 01:15.850
I got it, I'll let you ride.

01:16.310 --> 01:17.450
Really?

01:17.810 --> 01:22.060
Yeah, so you have to clean it with me.

01:22.110 --> 01:22.760
Okay!

01:28.310 --> 01:34.500
Dad said that only the person who cherishes the bike has the right to ride it.

01:35.360 --> 01:38.630
You seem to like Uncle's bike very much.

01:38.910 --> 01:39.530
Yeah.

01:39.910 --> 01:40.660
Kenji!

01:41.610 --> 01:43.300
It hurts!

01:43.950 --> 01:48.610
I gave this bike to you because you said you would clean it up.

01:48.640 --> 01:50.980
Why did you get lazy and make Nanami do the work?

01:51.510 --> 01:53.410
Uncle, I asked to do it.

01:53.410 --> 01:55.130
Nanami, you didn't do anything wrong.

01:55.420 --> 01:58.310
This is a problem between me and Kenji.

01:58.310 --> 02:00.360
Hey, listen to me!

02:00.400 --> 02:01.470
How dare you say that.

02:02.210 --> 02:04.010
It hurts!

02:04.510 --> 02:09.300
Bike Girl and Part-time Job

03:25.810 --> 03:26.900
Excuse me...

03:29.310 --> 03:30.830
W-Water...

03:31.110 --> 03:33.220
Huh? Ah...

03:36.610 --> 03:39.190
Water... W-Water...

03:40.010 --> 03:41.730
Here you go.

03:46.710 --> 03:50.040
Ken-chan. Ken-chan!

03:53.710 --> 03:56.860
What are you doing, Nanami-sensei?

04:06.110 --> 04:07.410
Here you go.

04:07.710 --> 04:09.370
Thank you very much.

04:09.510 --> 04:11.250
You really had a hard time just now, right?

04:11.310 --> 04:15.350
Riding a bike on a hot day such as this...

04:15.610 --> 04:17.650
The sun was okay...

04:19.910 --> 04:21.530
It was the earthworm.

04:23.610 --> 04:27.160
Well, we can't do anything about it. Nanami's dumb after all.

04:27.310 --> 04:29.380
Ken-chan, you're so mean.

04:29.910 --> 04:34.160
Well, giving an earthworm to someone you just met is really...

04:35.010 --> 04:37.610
Where are you going to go, Ayukawa-san?

04:37.910 --> 04:39.630
I didn't really plan for that.

04:40.010 --> 04:42.680
I was only wandering around here.

04:42.810 --> 04:45.320
Did you break your bike?

04:48.410 --> 04:52.890
Yeah, the engine has some problem.

04:53.210 --> 04:54.260
I see.

04:54.910 --> 04:55.510
Alright.

04:56.910 --> 04:58.310
Then, let's go?

04:58.810 --> 04:59.700
Where?

05:00.310 --> 05:01.100
My house.

05:09.310 --> 05:10.690
Just park there.

05:11.110 --> 05:12.750
O-Okay.

05:17.110 --> 05:19.040
How is it this year?

05:19.510 --> 05:23.440
Compared to fixing it, it was more troublesome getting money from Dad for parts.

05:23.510 --> 05:27.330
Fixing? You fixed this?

05:27.710 --> 05:31.620
Almost all the parts have been changed.

05:32.010 --> 05:33.380
I would rather say "I transformed it."

05:33.910 --> 05:36.020
Ken-chan is very skillful.

05:36.310 --> 05:39.630
Can you still ride it?

05:40.710 --> 05:44.000
But Ken-chan fixed it last year.

05:45.610 --> 05:49.410
But before summer vacation, it quit working again.

05:49.410 --> 05:50.360
Isn't that "un-fixable"?

05:51.410 --> 05:54.840
But, but, you can ride it every year.

05:55.110 --> 05:58.000
That means it breaks every year?

05:58.210 --> 05:59.800
That's even worse.

05:59.810 --> 06:01.410
But, but, but...

06:01.410 --> 06:02.890
That's enough!

06:03.610 --> 06:05.290
It's getting worse.

06:05.310 --> 06:08.370
Well, what am I doing here?

06:08.510 --> 06:11.110
Isn't that obvious? I'm here to fix your bike.

06:13.210 --> 06:14.140
What?

06:14.140 --> 06:16.490
But, is that going to be okay if I let you do it?

06:16.810 --> 06:17.730
Trust me.

06:18.270 --> 06:20.700
I'm not making poses for fixing a broken bike.

06:21.010 --> 06:22.430
Ken-chan, do your best.

06:22.710 --> 06:23.390
Okay.

06:23.810 --> 06:25.440
Is it really going to be okay?

06:54.110 --> 06:56.630
I did something bad. I can't make it up anymore.

06:57.210 --> 06:59.980
What did you do!?

07:02.210 --> 07:03.710
Accident... That was an accident.

07:04.010 --> 07:06.680
But it looks like it was a failure during operation.

07:08.510 --> 07:10.970
Well then, let's go to a bike dealer.

07:11.210 --> 07:13.320
But it's already closed.

07:13.610 --> 07:14.820
It's that late already?

07:15.010 --> 07:17.110
It's not even seven yet.

07:17.710 --> 07:19.920
This town is like that.

07:20.710 --> 07:22.700
That's why I hate the countryside.

07:22.810 --> 07:26.140
How are you going to pay for my bike?

07:31.710 --> 07:34.140
What are you all doing?

07:40.950 --> 07:42.020
It should be fine.

07:42.810 --> 07:44.380
Thank you very much.

07:44.610 --> 07:48.540
No, it was my son's fault after all.

07:52.410 --> 07:56.010
But it seems like you've accelerated it too much.

07:57.210 --> 08:00.770
Some of the parts are already broken. You have to change those.

08:04.310 --> 08:08.110
Yes, yes, yeah... thank you very much.

08:10.310 --> 08:11.410
What's wrong?

08:12.210 --> 08:14.910
It will take ten days for the parts to be shipped here.

08:17.910 --> 08:20.440
Wow, so expensive.

08:21.710 --> 08:24.500
Well, all you can do now is wait.

08:25.010 --> 08:29.100
Misora-chan, is it okay if you don't call your family?

08:29.280 --> 08:31.970
My parents are out of the country now.

08:32.510 --> 08:33.660
I see.

08:33.710 --> 08:35.720
Well, you can feel free to live in our house.

08:37.010 --> 08:37.930
But...

08:38.210 --> 08:39.890
Don't worry, it's fine.

08:40.610 --> 08:41.900
So, it's decided.

08:42.410 --> 08:44.790
Well...

08:46.910 --> 08:48.610
Sorry for the trouble.

08:55.510 --> 08:56.660
You finished?

08:58.010 --> 08:59.280
Yeah. Hey...

09:00.010 --> 09:00.660
What?

09:00.850 --> 09:03.000
Are there any places where I can work part time?

09:05.110 --> 09:05.940
Part time?

09:06.410 --> 09:08.740
We have to wait a few days until the parts ship here.

09:08.810 --> 09:11.020
And the repair cost is expensive too.

09:11.810 --> 09:13.740
Nanami's mother's tea store.

09:13.780 --> 09:16.290
I will pass on that.

09:16.710 --> 09:17.430
Why?

09:17.810 --> 09:20.820
I'm a little afraid of her.

09:21.410 --> 09:25.750
Well, yeah, she gave you an earthworm the first time she saw you. Of course you're not comfortable with it.

09:26.310 --> 09:27.430
Yeah...

09:27.610 --> 09:28.910
Tomorrow is Sunday.

09:29.610 --> 09:30.990
I'll go with you.

09:31.110 --> 09:31.920
Really?

09:32.810 --> 09:33.880
Thanks.

09:38.010 --> 09:40.470
What is this?

09:40.710 --> 09:41.750
Isn't that obvious?

09:42.110 --> 09:45.930
The first bed-battle poker competition!

09:48.010 --> 09:50.010
Misora will sleep in this room, right?

09:50.050 --> 09:56.870
Hey, you don't want to treat our guest well?

09:57.010 --> 09:58.890
No... But...

09:59.010 --> 10:01.950
Onii-chan, you aren't nice.

10:02.210 --> 10:04.260
Suzuka, even you are...

10:06.110 --> 10:10.210
Misora-chan thinks the bed is better than the couch, right?

10:10.610 --> 10:12.350
Thank you, Hikari-san.

10:12.910 --> 10:16.030
I am so touched by the kind-hearted people on my trip.

10:16.210 --> 10:19.410
We have to help each other when we're facing hard times, Misora-chan.

10:21.110 --> 10:22.460
Good, but...

10:23.810 --> 10:28.790
I know you don't want to. That's why we're using the game to make sure it's fair.

10:30.610 --> 10:32.140
That's true, but...

10:36.210 --> 10:37.770
We won!

10:40.810 --> 10:43.720
Well, Onii-chan, don't get cold here.

10:44.410 --> 10:46.210
Let's go, Misora-chan.

10:46.410 --> 10:47.110
Okay.

10:50.310 --> 10:52.040
Thanks for the bed.

10:55.210 --> 10:56.590
Huh?

11:23.910 --> 11:25.780
(To Onii-chan: I'm going to the morning practice, please take care of Misora. -Suzuka)
(Don't do anything bad!)

11:29.910 --> 11:30.980
It's time to get up.

11:33.710 --> 11:34.730
What the...?

11:39.910 --> 11:41.520
Is this a woman's true sleeping attitude?

11:42.310 --> 11:46.690
This countryside, even the cell phone isn't working.

11:47.710 --> 11:49.700
Is she really sleeping?

11:51.110 --> 11:52.240
Hey, it's time to get up.

11:53.600 --> 11:54.870
Hey...

11:58.410 --> 12:00.750
Hey, get up.

12:07.510 --> 12:09.920
This is bad...

12:18.910 --> 12:21.770
Ken-chan, good... morning...

12:24.710 --> 12:27.190
Ken-chan...

12:28.210 --> 12:30.140
Wait, calm down.

12:30.410 --> 12:31.550
You'll understand after I explain it to you.

12:32.310 --> 12:33.400
I've been mistaken!

12:37.310 --> 12:39.310
Ken-chan, you're an idiot!

12:39.310 --> 12:40.880
Nanami!

12:44.310 --> 12:45.680
It's morning already...

12:50.110 --> 12:52.990
So she is looking for a place to work.

12:59.310 --> 13:01.160
Hey, Hatano, hey.

13:02.160 --> 13:05.820
Hey, Kenji, who's that girl over there?

13:09.610 --> 13:12.330
This guy's out.

13:38.010 --> 13:39.420
Tomosaka-senpai!

13:51.710 --> 13:55.450
Sorry, about your work...

13:56.210 --> 13:58.070
Don't worry, we're just asking.

13:59.710 --> 14:01.790
No, I'm really sorry about it.

14:02.010 --> 14:03.670
Finally, you came over...

14:04.710 --> 14:07.120
No, we asked you all of a sudden.

14:07.910 --> 14:08.550
But...

14:13.810 --> 14:16.640
(Sign: Unicorn Beetle Nursery.)

14:36.710 --> 14:38.790
We didn't find anything in the end.

14:40.010 --> 14:42.910
No wonder... this is the countryside.

14:43.010 --> 14:43.900
What do you mean?

14:43.910 --> 14:47.960
Normally, you can't find a job in such a place like the Unicorn Beetle Nursery, right?

14:48.810 --> 14:50.310
It's very normal here, though.

14:51.010 --> 14:54.100
I can't believe that!

14:54.210 --> 14:57.440
I can at least find a job in a place like a karaoke room, a manga tearoom, or a grocery store, right?

14:58.210 --> 14:59.450
Maybe...

15:01.310 --> 15:02.970
I really want to go back now.

15:03.710 --> 15:05.140
Well, you go ahead first.

15:05.610 --> 15:06.390
What's wrong?

15:07.110 --> 15:08.390
I have to go somewhere.

15:10.810 --> 15:12.950
Ah, wait for me.

15:14.910 --> 15:16.850
You don't have to go with me.

15:17.010 --> 15:20.040
The key, only you have it, right?

15:20.310 --> 15:21.760
Oh, yeah.

15:26.110 --> 15:27.460
Nanami!

15:28.610 --> 15:29.490
Ken-chan.

15:42.110 --> 15:43.950
Can I ask, what can I do for you?

15:44.010 --> 15:46.140
Are you still mad at me about this morning?

15:46.460 --> 15:47.950
I don't mind at all.

15:48.410 --> 15:50.160
But it seems that you do care.

15:50.310 --> 15:52.390
Don't blame me like that.

15:56.910 --> 15:57.920
Is that all for today?

16:00.910 --> 16:02.900
Let's go back, Nanami.

16:11.010 --> 16:13.590
Today's tomatoes are pretty good.

16:14.110 --> 16:16.390
Well, I'm looking forward to tomorrow's lunch then.

16:16.910 --> 16:19.150
It can make pretty good spaghetti.

16:20.710 --> 16:22.760
Ayukawa-san, do you like tomatoes too?

16:24.110 --> 16:25.410
I don't hate them.

16:25.610 --> 16:26.900
That's good.

16:27.110 --> 16:31.260
Even though I'm a little tired... at least I planted some delicious vegetables.

16:33.710 --> 16:35.660
Do you want to give it a try, Ayukawa-san?

16:37.110 --> 16:39.740
Do you want to plant some vegetables by yourself?

16:39.960 --> 16:41.340
I'll pass.

16:41.410 --> 16:43.110
Don't be shy.

16:43.110 --> 16:44.240
It's not like that.

16:44.810 --> 16:48.070
I have to earn money for my bike's repair costs.

16:48.110 --> 16:50.060
Ah, I see.

16:50.810 --> 16:53.140
And, I'm not interested in this.

16:53.710 --> 16:54.670
I see.

16:55.210 --> 16:56.120
Misora.

16:56.610 --> 16:58.600
That's fine, anyway...

16:59.110 --> 17:02.080
But it's pretty fun to plant vegetables.

17:02.310 --> 17:04.910
And it's more delicious to eat the vegetables you've planted.

17:05.010 --> 17:08.140
The customers in the store will be happy too.

17:08.810 --> 17:11.540
But it does take time.

17:12.110 --> 17:15.100
You have to water the field and kill the pests everyday.

17:16.510 --> 17:19.030
It's very hard in the beginning.

17:20.210 --> 17:22.170
Same with Ken-chan's motorcycle.

17:22.510 --> 17:24.170
Ah, yeah.

17:24.410 --> 17:25.600
Can you still fix it?

17:25.710 --> 17:26.720
I still have to fix something.

17:40.310 --> 17:40.840
Hey...

17:42.610 --> 17:45.530
Why don't you buy a new bike?

17:46.210 --> 17:47.840
I never thought about it.

17:48.010 --> 17:50.310
But it would be hard to fix it, right?

17:50.340 --> 17:52.650
Yeah, but it's fun too.

17:52.910 --> 17:55.700
Why are you so persistent?

17:56.110 --> 17:59.160
My dad gave this to me.

17:59.510 --> 18:03.110
When I was a child, I watched my dad ride it.

18:03.110 --> 18:04.700
I thought, "That's so cool," I've always wanted this.

18:06.110 --> 18:09.570
After I begged him millions of times, I got my license. He finally gave it to me.

18:09.910 --> 18:14.890
But it got hard after that. It broke right after I got it.

18:17.410 --> 18:20.260
And it repeats every single year.

18:20.810 --> 18:23.830
Well, it has my memories with it anyway.

18:24.210 --> 18:27.240
What... that's just a waste of time.

18:27.710 --> 18:29.080
I've liked it for a long time.

18:29.610 --> 18:32.050
I still remember the day I fixed it.

18:32.610 --> 18:36.250
More accurately, I would say I'm still relying on it. It just feels like that.

18:38.210 --> 18:41.030
Even though it looks awkward... I still like it.

18:42.710 --> 18:44.730
You like this bike too, right?

18:45.310 --> 18:46.610
Of course.

18:47.110 --> 18:48.360
So you can understand, right?

18:49.310 --> 18:50.630
Sorry about yesterday.

18:51.710 --> 18:53.340
I messed up your bike.

18:54.010 --> 18:55.350
That's all right.

18:56.310 --> 18:57.550
Yeah, about your work.

18:58.410 --> 19:00.810
Don't worry, I'll look by myself.

19:01.510 --> 19:03.660
Well, good night.

19:17.510 --> 19:18.600
I'm home.

19:32.510 --> 19:33.730
Welcome.

19:36.910 --> 19:40.590
I, Ayukawa Misora, will be working here starting today.

19:40.710 --> 19:41.790
Nice to meet you.

19:43.910 --> 19:46.500
Ayukawa-san, please take care of this.

19:46.810 --> 19:47.530
Okay.

19:48.210 --> 19:50.470
Ah, you two, welcome back.

19:52.410 --> 19:53.830
H-O-W-E-V-E-R...

19:54.710 --> 19:56.630
I want to ask you.

19:57.110 --> 20:00.270
You two are... lovers, right?

20:00.410 --> 20:01.020
You...

20:01.310 --> 20:02.070
Two...

20:02.510 --> 20:03.820
You and you.

20:05.510 --> 20:07.790
What the heck are you talking about?

20:07.810 --> 20:12.710
That's... I and... Ken-chan are... lovers...

20:12.710 --> 20:14.440
Yeah, that's so rude!

20:14.610 --> 20:15.980
I'm so embarrassed... so embarrassed...

20:18.810 --> 20:20.990
Yeah, yeah, thank you for having me.

20:25.880 --> 20:28.730
Today's field work was very hard too.

20:28.780 --> 20:30.050
Nanami!

20:30.180 --> 20:31.980
Ah, Hikari-chan.

20:32.040 --> 20:34.330
What's that giant watermelon?

20:34.360 --> 20:37.490
That's a new Nanami special.

20:37.580 --> 20:40.240
Wait! It's coming this way!

20:40.580 --> 20:44.960
Ah, Nanami's having a big problem now!

20:45.280 --> 20:47.670
Hmm, it's so heavy.

20:48.580 --> 20:52.090
Next on Lamune:
Two Persons' Bond and Swaying Feelings

20:52.280 --> 20:53.580
What is that?

20:56.590 --> 21:00.950
I remember the first time you looked at me.

21:01.850 --> 21:02.960
Konoe-san, an order.

21:03.990 --> 21:05.680
Konoe-san, it's finished.

21:05.810 --> 21:06.750
Give it to me.

21:06.890 --> 21:07.870
The customer wants to pay.

21:08.010 --> 21:09.110
Okay...

21:09.270 --> 21:11.710
Waitress work is very hard.

21:12.360 --> 21:15.170
Ayukawa-san you are looking well.

21:15.330 --> 21:16.220
One more time.

21:16.590 --> 21:17.650
Next time on Lamune:

21:18.020 --> 21:19.970
Two Persons' Bond and Swaying Feelings

21:20.370 --> 21:22.900
Welcome!

21:23.230 --> 21:24.850
You look really tired!

21:27.720 --> 21:30.590
Welcome back, master.

21:31.180 --> 21:34.560
Why do I have to be a waitress?

21:35.490 --> 21:38.400
Misora-chan, we are short on help right now...

21:38.690 --> 21:40.490
Please go clean the table.

21:41.080 --> 21:41.650
Sure.

21:42.960 --> 21:43.950
Pardon me.

21:51.930 --> 21:54.570
I am very sorry Master!

21:55.920 --> 21:56.670
Owww.

21:58.240 --> 22:00.700
Are you all right, Misora-san?

22:02.180 --> 22:03.300
Thanks!

22:08.210 --> 22:10.580
Nanami Onee-sama is really something.

22:21.880 --> 22:26.880
 Thanks to the following:
Ripper: TCT66; Original Timer: nanaya; Original Typesetter: kiasushou; Original Chinese Subs for Extra Scenes: Fino; English Subs: C1Anime

22:23.480 --> 22:26.880
I'm so envious of Misora...
